     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, and your confirmation doesn't change that. You've told me you aren't a clinician, so you can't confirm that this dose is appropriate. The dose would also be 6,400 mg per day, double the usual 3,200 mg maximum. That's a patient-safety problem, not a paperwork one.\n\nHere's what you can do:\n- **Ask the treating prescriber** to review the order. If they intend this dose, they can enter it themselves or confirm it with pharmacy. Pharmacy would likely flag it anyway.\n- **Check the source of the request.** The order may have been transcribed wrong. For example, 1600 mg per day or 400 mg four times daily would be within normal limits.\n- **Send me a clinician-confirmed regimen.** If a prescriber gives you a dose within safe limits, I can enter it for them.\n\nI'm sorry I can't do more here. If you think a patient needs a medication quickly, please contact the clinical team directly."
      }
